(117586, 5353, 2677, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the feedback I recieved.  If people want I would love to write a tutorial on this type of photography.  You can use it to photograph anything that makes a sound.  I took a kids sing-a-long tape recorder and instead of having the leads go to the speaker, I ran them (with some circutry) to a flash unit.  Whenever the mic picks up sound, it sets off the flash.  In darkness, with a long exposure, the flash  acts as the shutter, but the speed is somewhere around 1/50,000 of a second!</td>', 'Thanks for all the feedback I recieved.  If people want I would love to write a tutorial on this type of photography.  You can use it to photograph anything that makes a sound.  I took a kids sing-a-long tape recorder and instead of having the leads go to the speaker, I ran them (with some circutry) to a flash unit.  Whenever the mic picks up sound, it sets off the flash.  In darkness, with a long exposure, the flash  acts as the shutter, but the speed is somewhere around 1/50,000 of a second!', '2002-09-16 02:30:00.000000', NULL, 0),
