(117848, 5374, 133, '<td valign="top">A new take on vegetables! LOL.</td>', 'A new take on vegetables! LOL.', '2002-09-11 10:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(117849, 5374, 2337, '<td valign="top">At first glance I marked this low and hated this shot, thinking it was a ''pull from the freezer, thrown on the counter'' job... As I go through for my second look, I''m noticing that this is actually rather well done...  The things that would have improved it most (for me) would have been a waste of food... If the bags were opened with the veggies spilling out, it would have been a better shot, but way too wasteful (unless you were really hungry)... So within those constrants, I would only offer two more suggestions... If the top bag had been at an angle similar to the bottom bag (coming at more of a 45 degree angle) I think it would have worked better for me... Second, notice tghe shadow beneath the bags?  If you had 2 light sorces coming from different directions, that would have been more controllable.  I just noticed a 3rd thing... If you have placed these on a black piece of construction paper (or similiar dark background) I think it might have helped quite a bit...  Of course, this is all just my slant on it... It''s how you feel about the shot that truely counts.  I''m bumping your score from 4 to 6 ~ myqyl ~</td>', 'At first glance I marked this low and hated this shot, thinking it was a ''pull from the freezer, thrown on the counter'' job... As I go through for my second look, I''m noticing that this is actually rather well done...  The things that would have improved it most (for me) would have been a waste of food... If the bags were opened with the veggies spilling out, it would have been a better shot, but way too wasteful (unless you were really hungry)... So within those constrants, I would only offer two more suggestions... If the top bag had been at an angle similar to the bottom bag (coming at more of a 45 degree angle) I think it would have worked better for me... Second, notice tghe shadow beneath the bags?  If you had 2 light sorces coming from different directions, that would have been more controllable.  I just noticed a 3rd thing... If you have placed these on a black piece of construction paper (or similiar dark background) I think it might have helped quite a bit...  Of course, this is all just my slant on it... It''s how you feel about the shot that truely counts.  I''m bumping your score from 4 to 6 ~ myqyl ~', '2002-09-11 11:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(117850, 5374, 2172, '<td valign="top">Being honest - NOT to offend.  This doesn''t do anything for me.  I''m looking at this and what I think is...well, someone took 3 bags of frozen veggies, layered them on the counter, stook over them and pressed the shutter button with the flash.  Although I personally don''t see bags of frozen veggies that appealing, perhaps there are a few things that could help this.  I would definately go for a different angle, perhaps set the camer on the counter, may use a shallow dof, maybe stack them evenly and shoot down the center of the even edges of the bags.  Also, need to alter the lighting - turn the flash off and use a household lamp...or try Hokies ghetto studio setup (check in the threads).  This is just my opinion.   3<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Being honest - NOT to offend.  This doesn''t do anything for me.  I''m looking at this and what I think is...well, someone took 3 bags of frozen veggies, layered them on the counter, stook over them and pressed the shutter button with the flash.  Although I personally don''t see bags of frozen veggies that appealing, perhaps there are a few things that could help this.  I would definately go for a different angle, perhaps set the camer on the counter, may use a shallow dof, maybe stack them evenly and shoot down the center of the even edges of the bags.  Also, need to alter the lighting - turn the flash off and use a household lamp...or try Hokies ghetto studio setup (check in the threads).  This is just my opinion.   3Ruthann', '2002-09-11 17:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(117851, 5374, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background7,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing8,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 7,<br/>Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool<br/>You should have opened at least one of the bags and let some of the veggie dribble out.  Good Luck</td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background7,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing8,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 7,Total Averaged Rating7.   AutoolYou should have opened at least one of the bags and let some of the veggie dribble out.  Good Luck', '2002-09-11 23:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
