(117875, 5375, 3454, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and use of colour. Not sure if the focus and weaker lighting on the strawberry was intentional?</td>', 'Nice composition and use of colour. Not sure if the focus and weaker lighting on the strawberry was intentional?', '2002-09-15 14:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(117876, 5375, 255, '<td valign="top">Composition/Content: I am quite fond of fruit macros for some reason! I rated it high during the challenge. I like the way the lines and curves work together, but the most striking thing about this photo is the contrast of colors. The colors work nicely together, but the main problem I have is the focus of the berry. To me, it is as much the subject of this photo as the kiwi, so should share the focus. Right now it seems to be less of a focal point and more of just a contrasting object in the frame. <br/><br/>Background/lighting:<br/><br/>The white background works well here, although the lighting seems off on the berry. My eyes are drawn to the right side of the kiwi where the light hits it, but then flow over to the berry, where it just sort of fades. Maybe a secondary light would have been nice here.<br/><br/>Overall, I like this. I know with my fruit macros, I have to take many pics with many different angles to get the right focus and composition. I think the most important thing with something like this is the focus--perhaps playing around with getting closer w/ less zoom and vice versa. Keep in mind that I am NOT saying that everything in the frame should be in focus--just the focal point! :) For example, given the way you cropped the shot, you might have started the focus in the front corner and let the DOF fade into the background. Or maybe just incorporated more than just the left edge of the berry---bringing more of the berry''s texture into view. Just food for thought! ;)</td>', 'Composition/Content: I am quite fond of fruit macros for some reason! I rated it high during the challenge. I like the way the lines and curves work together, but the most striking thing about this photo is the contrast of colors. The colors work nicely together, but the main problem I have is the focus of the berry. To me, it is as much the subject of this photo as the kiwi, so should share the focus. Right now it seems to be less of a focal point and more of just a contrasting object in the frame. Background/lighting:The white background works well here, although the lighting seems off on the berry. My eyes are drawn to the right side of the kiwi where the light hits it, but then flow over to the berry, where it just sort of fades. Maybe a secondary light would have been nice here.Overall, I like this. I know with my fruit macros, I have to take many pics with many different angles to get the right focus and composition. I think the most important thing with something like this is the focus--perhaps playing around with getting closer w/ less zoom and vice versa. Keep in mind that I am NOT saying that everything in the frame should be in focus--just the focal point! :) For example, given the way you cropped the shot, you might have started the focus in the front corner and let the DOF fade into the background. Or maybe just incorporated more than just the left edge of the berry---bringing more of the berry''s texture into view. Just food for thought! ;)', '2002-11-24 19:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(117877, 5376, 327, '<td valign="top">Coco....lol. Cute idea. The photo is OOF and the light is a bit harsh. Justine</td>', 'Coco....lol. Cute idea. The photo is OOF and the light is a bit harsh. Justine', '2002-09-09 10:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
