(120290, 5528, 2798, '<td valign="top">Love the light on this shot. Nice framing too. 8 - floyd</td>', 'Love the light on this shot. Nice framing too. 8 - floyd', '2002-09-12 06:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120291, 5528, 3087, '<td valign="top">Good strong colour and great to have all the shadow in shot. Background needs a little more light (for my tastes). Cropped a little tight at the top. <br/>Kavey</td>', 'Good strong colour and great to have all the shadow in shot. Background needs a little more light (for my tastes). Cropped a little tight at the top. Kavey', '2002-09-13 06:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120292, 5528, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background6,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing6,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 5,<br/>Total Averaged Rating6.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background6,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing6,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 5,Total Averaged Rating6.   Autool', '2002-09-14 00:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120293, 5528, 3903, '<td valign="top">Very good use of ligh and shadow</td>', 'Very good use of ligh and shadow', '2002-09-14 10:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120294, 5528, 1280, '<td valign="top">beautiful, with great coloring.  Good luck in the callenge.  Gracious aka Grayce</td>', 'beautiful, with great coloring.  Good luck in the callenge.  Gracious aka Grayce', '2002-09-14 12:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120295, 5528, 1054, '<td valign="top">Fruit, and excellent lighting.  The fade from white to black is refreshing after looking at so many solid backgrounds.  Please share how you lit this!</td>', 'Fruit, and excellent lighting.  The fade from white to black is refreshing after looking at so many solid backgrounds.  Please share how you lit this!', '2002-09-15 11:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120296, 5528, 4162, '<td valign="top">Critique by Natasha<br/><br/>Composition-Content<br/>I think that the placing of the tomato could have been slightly lower in the picture. The shadows add depth to this  shot and add interest but the "face" of the tomato leads the viewer out of the right side of the picture. Otherwise, the rule of thirds were followed to your advantage and also leaves enough space for background detail. The colour here is lovely, really creates a ripe, edible tomato.<br/><br/>Background<br/>The background here helps the tomato to stand out, but in my opinion it is too dark at the top of the picture.  It fades into light but not equally on both sides, this does however complement the natural tilt of the tomoato.  The use of shadows adds depth and they would stand out more if the top of the picture were brighter.There is one stray bit of black fluff to the left of the tomato which is a bit distracting. <br/><br/>Camera Work-Technical<br/><br/>Focus is great here.  The lighting on the tomato really adds to the colour, the golden specs are great. The one flash highlight on the tomato slightly attracts the viewers attention, a bounced flash could help here. <br/><br/>Digital Processing<br/>The edges of the tomato could benefit from a little sharpening, but I think this is up to you! The tomato is not a perfect shape anyway, so looks more natural the way you shot it.<br/><br/>My Opinion<br/>My first impression was OK, bu t I really appreciate the colours of the tomato, especially the nice golden specs!  I am not too keen on the background, personally I think a little more light would be good.  Overall, you definitely made this tomato look worth eating , a great job!<br/><br/><br/></td>', 'Critique by NatashaComposition-ContentI think that the placing of the tomato could have been slightly lower in the picture. The shadows add depth to this  shot and add interest but the "face" of the tomato leads the viewer out of the right side of the picture. Otherwise, the rule of thirds were followed to your advantage and also leaves enough space for background detail. The colour here is lovely, really creates a ripe, edible tomato.BackgroundThe background here helps the tomato to stand out, but in my opinion it is too dark at the top of the picture.  It fades into light but not equally on both sides, this does however complement the natural tilt of the tomoato.  The use of shadows adds depth and they would stand out more if the top of the picture were brighter.There is one stray bit of black fluff to the left of the tomato which is a bit distracting. Camera Work-TechnicalFocus is great here.  The lighting on the tomato really adds to the colour, the golden specs are great. The one flash highlight on the tomato slightly attracts the viewers attention, a bounced flash could help here. Digital ProcessingThe edges of the tomato could benefit from a little sharpening, but I think this is up to you! The tomato is not a perfect shape anyway, so looks more natural the way you shot it.My OpinionMy first impression was OK, bu t I really appreciate the colours of the tomato, especially the nice golden specs!  I am not too keen on the background, personally I think a little more light would be good.  Overall, you definitely made this tomato look worth eating , a great job!', '2002-11-24 21:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(120297, 5531, 2361, '<td valign="top">I like the contrast here, but the ctop is too close for comfort.  5 Jak</td>', 'I like the contrast here, but the ctop is too close for comfort.  5 Jak', '2002-09-09 01:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120298, 5531, 3280, '<td valign="top">I love the title and composition but the colors seem a bit too bland.</td>', 'I love the title and composition but the colors seem a bit too bland.', '2002-09-09 12:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120299, 5531, 1041, '<td valign="top">you''ve got some funky lighting going on here, or you''ve played with the contrast too much.  i think a more plain background would have worked better for me, and either cropping off more than just the end of the banana or having everything in the frame.  this way, it looks accidental to me. -- gr8photos.</td>', 'you''ve got some funky lighting going on here, or you''ve played with the contrast too much.  i think a more plain background would have worked better for me, and either cropping off more than just the end of the banana or having everything in the frame.  this way, it looks accidental to me. -- gr8photos.', '2002-09-09 16:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120300, 5531, 2337, '<td valign="top">At first I scored this low.  The contrast and lighting seemed harsh.  They are still harsh, but it''s growing on me.</td>', 'At first I scored this low.  The contrast and lighting seemed harsh.  They are still harsh, but it''s growing on me.', '2002-09-10 20:19:00.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(120301, 5531, 3112, '<td valign="top">Good use of title to make it go. Composition is good, but lighting might be better.</td>', 'Good use of title to make it go. Composition is good, but lighting might be better.', '2002-09-11 00:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120302, 5531, 835, '<td valign="top">the stripper looks a little worn on the edges.  Time for a fresh one.  :)<br/>I would prefer softer lighting.</td>', 'the stripper looks a little worn on the edges.  Time for a fresh one.  :)I would prefer softer lighting.', '2002-09-12 00:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120303, 5531, 811, '<td valign="top">Funny title!  It looks like you have used a lot of contrast (?) on this, which i think gives it an edgy feel.  That is effective, I think.  The colors are a little bland to me though.  Maybe a different background color to give it some contrast. karmat</td>', 'Funny title!  It looks like you have used a lot of contrast (?) on this, which i think gives it an edgy feel.  That is effective, I think.  The colors are a little bland to me though.  Maybe a different background color to give it some contrast. karmat', '2002-09-13 14:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120304, 5531, 1037, '<td valign="top">I like the composition of this, and the colour processing you did gives it an interesting texture. It departs a bit from the vibrancy of most of the other photos in this challenge and looks more sober and serious. I like that.</td>', 'I like the composition of this, and the colour processing you did gives it an interesting texture. It departs a bit from the vibrancy of most of the other photos in this challenge and looks more sober and serious. I like that.', '2002-09-14 11:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120305, 5531, 2858, '<td valign="top">Great use of light. Love the tonal range and subdued colouring.</td>', 'Great use of light. Love the tonal range and subdued colouring.', '2002-09-14 12:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120306, 5531, 1280, '<td valign="top">I like your use of texture here.  Good luck in the callenge.  Gracious aka Grayce</td>', 'I like your use of texture here.  Good luck in the callenge.  Gracious aka Grayce', '2002-09-14 12:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120307, 5531, 671, '<td valign="top">bland coloring.</td>', 'bland coloring.', '2002-09-14 12:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120308, 5531, 3672, '<td valign="top">The lighting in this photograph does not flatter your subject.</td>', 'The lighting in this photograph does not flatter your subject.', '2002-09-14 13:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
