(120433, 5541, 772, '<td valign="top">Conceptually, this is a very good photo... i wish the image quality was better.  i believe this shot probalby needed a tripod to stabilize the camera.  Camera shake causes this effect.  photographing in darker places with no flash causes the camer to use a longer shutter speed and any minor vibrations in the camera can cause blur like this... - jmsetzler</td>', 'Conceptually, this is a very good photo... i wish the image quality was better.  i believe this shot probalby needed a tripod to stabilize the camera.  Camera shake causes this effect.  photographing in darker places with no flash causes the camer to use a longer shutter speed and any minor vibrations in the camera can cause blur like this... - jmsetzler', '2002-09-09 16:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(120434, 5541, 1005, '<td valign="top">Good idea!  Is the blur on purpose?  (why?)  I think the set up was too dark for the camera to focus properly, maybe.  6 Swash</td>', 'Good idea!  Is the blur on purpose?  (why?)  I think the set up was too dark for the camera to focus properly, maybe.  6 Swash', '2002-09-09 17:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
