(120522, 5547, 327, '<td valign="top">Salad for Caesar<br/>Olympus E20<br/> <br/>Interestingly enough it appears I didn''t vote on this photo. &amp;lt;?&amp;gt; I think I was out of town during that challenge. <br/>This photo is colorful and it fits the challenge well along with good focus and lighting.<br/> <br/>The weakest area is the composition. It''s sparse and looks stiff. Also the proportions are too small for the top of the pillar. Maybe large green lettuce leaves, a knife, or water would of filled in some of the negative area. The color is so nice here but there isn''t enough of it. The background is very white as is the pillar making the upper left look a bit over exposed. This could easily be corrected.<br/>I will also add,..... had I taken this shot I''d of dropped the camera down about a foot getting closer to the subject. My over all opinion of this photo is good. <br/></td>', 'Salad for CaesarOlympus E20 Interestingly enough it appears I didn''t vote on this photo. &lt;?&gt; I think I was out of town during that challenge. This photo is colorful and it fits the challenge well along with good focus and lighting. The weakest area is the composition. It''s sparse and looks stiff. Also the proportions are too small for the top of the pillar. Maybe large green lettuce leaves, a knife, or water would of filled in some of the negative area. The color is so nice here but there isn''t enough of it. The background is very white as is the pillar making the upper left look a bit over exposed. This could easily be corrected.I will also add,..... had I taken this shot I''d of dropped the camera down about a foot getting closer to the subject. My over all opinion of this photo is good. ', '2002-11-24 18:07:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(120523, 5548, 1041, '<td valign="top">good idea here, but on my monitor this looks out of focus all the way through.  i''m wondering whether that''s deliberate for some reason that i don''t get (i''d like to see something in focus, my eyes keep searching around), or whether maybe you got too close for your camera to be able to focus ... happens to me a lot with mine, because it indicates that it has focused even if it hasn''t. -- gr8photos</td>', 'good idea here, but on my monitor this looks out of focus all the way through.  i''m wondering whether that''s deliberate for some reason that i don''t get (i''d like to see something in focus, my eyes keep searching around), or whether maybe you got too close for your camera to be able to focus ... happens to me a lot with mine, because it indicates that it has focused even if it hasn''t. -- gr8photos', '2002-09-09 12:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
