(120746, 5558, 3087, '<td valign="top">Hi Meggie,<br/>Further comment on your photo as requested. Apologies for not making it earlier, was pressed for time during voting on this challenge. :)<br/>I like the subject matter of this photo - the composition with the half orange against the glass is very pleasing. I also like the moistness on the fruit and the wetness of the glass. <br/>I think it''s cropped a little tight all around, not much but just a little. I find that the background doesn''t give enough contrast against the main colour of the fruit/ juice to make the overall image zing out a little more.<br/>Hope this is of some help,<br/>Kavey</td>', 'Hi Meggie,Further comment on your photo as requested. Apologies for not making it earlier, was pressed for time during voting on this challenge. :)I like the subject matter of this photo - the composition with the half orange against the glass is very pleasing. I also like the moistness on the fruit and the wetness of the glass. I think it''s cropped a little tight all around, not much but just a little. I find that the background doesn''t give enough contrast against the main colour of the fruit/ juice to make the overall image zing out a little more.Hope this is of some help,Kavey', '2002-09-16 09:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(120747, 5558, 2867, '<td valign="top">thanks a ton all!  My best score but far from my best place-oh well.  I thought about a black background but i was hoping the white background with the orangish tint from the juice would tie it all together and make it blend.  Thanks for everything once again!</td>', 'thanks a ton all!  My best score but far from my best place-oh well.  I thought about a black background but i was hoping the white background with the orangish tint from the juice would tie it all together and make it blend.  Thanks for everything once again!', '2002-09-16 09:57:00.000000', NULL, 0),
