(121033, 5572, 3372, '<td valign="top">Great shot!  Either you got this one on the first attempt or you ate a lot of cereal and berries this week.</td>', 'Great shot!  Either you got this one on the first attempt or you ate a lot of cereal and berries this week.', '2002-09-15 17:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(121034, 5572, 2221, '<td valign="top">Hey, ich bin wohl einer der wenigen die den Titel verstehen ;-) Gute Idee mit der Milch! Schoener Farbkontrast Weiss/Rot/Gruen. Ich haette wahrscheinlich nur 3 Erdbeeren genommen, weil ich Asymmetrie spannender finde. Etwas schade, dass die Milch aus dem Bild schwappt, aber insgesamt ein gutes stop motion Photo. -stephan</td>', 'Hey, ich bin wohl einer der wenigen die den Titel verstehen ;-) Gute Idee mit der Milch! Schoener Farbkontrast Weiss/Rot/Gruen. Ich haette wahrscheinlich nur 3 Erdbeeren genommen, weil ich Asymmetrie spannender finde. Etwas schade, dass die Milch aus dem Bild schwappt, aber insgesamt ein gutes stop motion Photo. -stephan', '2002-09-15 19:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(121035, 5572, 312, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for the comments this week. Yes, I know I left the "green bits" on, but I thought the strawberries would look funny without them, and I liked the added color. The title is German and translates to "Four Strawberries." I''m not German, and I don''t speak German, but when I''m trying to come up with witty titles for my pictures, my roommate is always suggesting that I translate a normal boring title into Spanish for added artistic effect. "Cuatro Fresas" didn''t really have a great ring to it, so I went with German. I''ve always loved the sound of the language, anyway.<br/><br/>If anyone is interested, I edited the background and some of the blurs of this shot for a print quality version. I''ve posted it here: //www.photosig.com/viewphoto.php?id=307160<br/><br/>Thanks again for all the kind comments.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for the comments this week. Yes, I know I left the "green bits" on, but I thought the strawberries would look funny without them, and I liked the added color. The title is German and translates to "Four Strawberries." I''m not German, and I don''t speak German, but when I''m trying to come up with witty titles for my pictures, my roommate is always suggesting that I translate a normal boring title into Spanish for added artistic effect. "Cuatro Fresas" didn''t really have a great ring to it, so I went with German. I''ve always loved the sound of the language, anyway.If anyone is interested, I edited the background and some of the blurs of this shot for a print quality version. I''ve posted it here: //www.photosig.com/viewphoto.php?id=307160Thanks again for all the kind comments.', '2002-09-16 20:06:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(121036, 5572, 2221, '<td valign="top">Ooops. I thought that you speak german when using such a title and somehow I felt invited to comment in german. But it wouldn''t be fair to all the other non-german users who look through other people comments, either. Sorry about that. So here is the translation:<br/>"Hey, i''m probably the only one who gets the title ;-) Good idea with the milk! Nice contrast of colours white/red/green. I probaly would have used only three strawberries, because I find asymmetry more exciting. A little sad that the milk spills out of the photo, but overall a good stop motion photo."<br/></td>', 'Ooops. I thought that you speak german when using such a title and somehow I felt invited to comment in german. But it wouldn''t be fair to all the other non-german users who look through other people comments, either. Sorry about that. So here is the translation:"Hey, i''m probably the only one who gets the title ;-) Good idea with the milk! Nice contrast of colours white/red/green. I probaly would have used only three strawberries, because I find asymmetry more exciting. A little sad that the milk spills out of the photo, but overall a good stop motion photo."', '2002-09-16 22:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(121037, 5572, 312, '<td valign="top">stephan - i enjoyed your comment, and plugged it into babelfish.altavista.com which actually gave a half-way decent translation for once. i actually thank you for commenting in German, because it just makes things so much more interesting :)</td>', 'stephan - i enjoyed your comment, and plugged it into babelfish.altavista.com which actually gave a half-way decent translation for once. i actually thank you for commenting in German, because it just makes things so much more interesting :)', '2002-09-17 00:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(121038, 5572, 2221, '<td valign="top">Hehe, but considering the awful and sometimes very funny translations of Babelfish, I''ll stick to English though. I think even my German-to-English is better than Babelfish''s ;-)</td>', 'Hehe, but considering the awful and sometimes very funny translations of Babelfish, I''ll stick to English though. I think even my German-to-English is better than Babelfish''s ;-)', '2002-09-17 07:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
