(121369, 5588, 2244, '<td valign="top">I wanted to thank everyone for the all the comments!  To those who said landscape would be better, I agree....it''s just that I had this reflection thing going so I didn''t do any landscape takes.  Good luck to everyone in the "negative" challenge! Jakob</td>', 'I wanted to thank everyone for the all the comments!  To those who said landscape would be better, I agree....it''s just that I had this reflection thing going so I didn''t do any landscape takes.  Good luck to everyone in the "negative" challenge! Jakob', '2002-09-16 15:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(121370, 5588, 3575, '<td valign="top">Just toss this comment on the top of your already high pile of praise. Great concept, execution and photographers talent. This is a beautiful, timely tribute. Those few who feel you shouldn''t have "used" 9/11 only need to go into the grocery store to see the commercialization of the 9/11 tragedy -- bouquet after bouquet of red white &amp; blue carnations, red, white &amp; blue roses with glitter -- red, white and blue cookies! You''d think it was the 4th of July!  Your tribute was very reverent and I applaud you - there''s no comparison.</td>', 'Just toss this comment on the top of your already high pile of praise. Great concept, execution and photographers talent. This is a beautiful, timely tribute. Those few who feel you shouldn''t have "used" 9/11 only need to go into the grocery store to see the commercialization of the 9/11 tragedy -- bouquet after bouquet of red white & blue carnations, red, white & blue roses with glitter -- red, white and blue cookies! You''d think it was the 4th of July!  Your tribute was very reverent and I applaud you - there''s no comparison.', '2002-09-16 19:21:00.000000', NULL, 0),
